      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Additional Supplemental Information</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>PART I, LINE 2 PROCEDURES FOR MONITORING USE OF GRANTS FUNDS IN U.S.THE ORGANIZATION OPERATES A SCHOLARSHIP PROGRAM TO PROVIDE FINANCIAL SUPPORT FOR COLLEGE TO HIGH-ACHIEVING HIGH SCHOOL STUDENTS IN GREATER SAN DIEGO COUNTY WHO HAVE APPLIED FOR AND MET THE SET CRITERIA OF ACADEMIC PERFORMANCE, COMMUNITY SERVICE AND RECOMMENDATIONS BY COMMUNITY LEADERS. THE ORGANIZATION'S BOARD OF DIRECTORS OVERSEES THE SCHOLARSHIP SELECTION PROCESS AND GRANT ADMINISTRATION PROCEDURES. THE ORGANIZATION MAINTAINS RECORDS ON ALL SCHOLARSHIP RECIPIENTS, INCLUDING APPLICATION MATERIALS AND PAYMENT RECORDS. RECIPIENTS ARE INVITED TO ATTEND THE ORGANIZATION'S ANNUAL SCHOLARSHIP RECEPTION WHERE THEY ARE PRESENTED WITH THEIR SCHOLARSHIP AWARDS. THE ORGANIZATION MAY RESCIND ANY UNDISTRIBUTED SCHOLARSHIP AWARD IF THE ORGANIZATION BECOMES AWARE OF ANY MISAPPROPRIATION OF FUNDS OR FRAUDULENT ACTIONS BY THE RECIPIENTIN THEIR APPLICATION MATERIALS. ADHERENCE TO THESE PROCEDURES ENABLE THE ORGANIZATION TO UPHOLD ITS CHARITABLE OBJECTIVES AND MAINTAIN ACCOUNTABILITY OVER SCHOLARSHIP EXPENDITURES</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
    </IRS990ScheduleI>
